---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import Terminal from '../components/Terminal.astro';
---
<Base title="Medallion architecture" description="How Lakelet fits a standard bronze / silver / gold medallion architecture: same layers, same dbt project, same Iceberg tables in your bucket — but the laptop does most of the work and only the runs that don't fit burst to the cloud.">


  <div class="top">
    <div class="eyebrow"># use case · medallion architecture</div>
    <h1 class="page">Bronze, silver, gold. Same layers, one laptop.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Most lakehouses are organised the same way: raw data lands in bronze, gets cleaned into silver, and is shaped into gold tables people actually query. Lakelet doesn't change that pattern. It changes where each layer runs and what it costs. The layers are Iceberg tables in your bucket, the transformations are the dbt project you already have, and the laptop does everything the gauge says it can.</p>
    <div class="key"><span><i class="g"></i>Runs here</span><span><i class="y"></i>Runs here, slowly</span><span><i class="r"></i>Needs more machine → burst</span><span><i class="lap"></i>Laptop</span><span><i class="wk"></i>Ephemeral worker</span></div>
  </div>

